NAME

ulibFreeFileData - Frees the memory used by a file's description


SYNOPSIS

void ulibFreeFileData(struct FileCat *f)
                             a0


DESCRIPTION

This function frees the memory occupied by a file's description.

If <f->Description> is a NULL pointer, then no action is taken.  Otherwise,
Xenolink will free the description memory.

This function will set <f->Description> to NULL after it has freed the
memory.


NOTES

Xenolink frees the memory with the following command:

   FreeMem(f->Description, strlen(f->Description)+1);

That is, the amount of memory freed is the string length of the file
description, plus one, for the null terminator.  This information will be
important to you if you are specifically allocating file description memory,
without using the ulibStoreFileData() function.  It is not recommended that
you do this.


SEE ALSO

ulibStoreFileData
